# BilbyBots — Supabase + Google OAuth config
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# Used for local dev AND the Vercel web deploy (push these values to Vercel
# env vars — see scripts/vercel-env.sh and docs/specs/vercel-deploy.md).
#
# How to get these (one-time setup, ~10 min):
#   1. Create a free Supabase project: https://supabase.com/dashboard (free tier: 500MB DB, 50k MAU)
#   2. Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API:
#        EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL        = https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#        EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   = the "anon" public key (safe for clients, RLS protects data)
#   3. Auth → Sign In / Up → Providers → Google: add the Google Client ID/Secret (see docs/specs/auth-setup.md)
#   4. Auth → URL Configuration → add redirect URLs (native + web) from docs/specs/auth-setup.md
#
# For native OAuth the app needs the OAuth client IDs registered in Google Cloud Console:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID   = <ios client id>
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID = <android client id>
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID   = <web client id>
# (These are set in Google Cloud Console "OAuth 2.0 Client IDs" — see the guide.)
# If you use Supabase's hosted Google provider, only the two SUPABASE_* vars above
# plus the Supabase-side Google client config are strictly required.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google OAuth client IDs (for native deep-link sign-in; optional on web)
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
